% BAB/L/021, Science Museum Group Collection, document aa110001687.
% Cover 222/599 ("No 21", "15 Aug 1840"); the opened sheet 222/600 with the
% table and, at the right, "Variable Cards"; the back 340/323, blank but for
% two small marks at the left edge. Read from the zoom images at full
% resolution. See sources/notes/L021.md.
%
% Babbage writes the accents before the letter: 'a is a′, ''b is b″; ∂ is
% written d. "C'b" over a small 0 (a complement laid and given back in the
% same operation) is C(b') 0; "0" over a letter (given off and retained) is
% "0 x".

Sheet BAB/L/021
No. 21
Date 15 Aug 1840          "15 Aug 1840"   % cover
Title "Reduction of the four Equations"
Image 222/599 cover: "Reduction of the four Equations aw + bx + cy + ∂z + e = 0, 'aw + 'bx + 'cy + '∂z + 'e = 0, ''aw + ''bx + ''cy + ''∂z + ''e = 0, '''aw + '''bx + '''cy + '''∂z + '''e = 0 to three others viz Bx + Cy + Dz + E = 0, 'Bx + 'Cy + 'Dz + 'E = 0, ''Bx + ''Cy + ''Dz + ''E = 0"
Image 222/600 the table, the left-hand list of operands, and the variable cards
Image 340/323 back: blank

Letters a b c d e a' b' c' d' e' a'' b'' c'' d'' e'' a''' b''' c''' d''' e'''

% Store headings: v1 0, v2 b, v3 c, v4 ∂, v5 e; v6 0, v7 'b … v10 'e; v11 0,
% v12 ''b … v15 ''e; v16 0, v17 '''b … v20 '''e; v21 a, v22 0, v23 'a, v24 0,
% v25 ''a, v26 0, v27 '''a, v28 0; v29 to v32 with no heading. The
% multipliers stand apart from their equations, each with an empty column
% beside it for its complement. v16, v31 and v32 are never used.
Store v2 = b, v3 = c, v4 = d, v5 = e, v7 = b', v8 = c', v9 = d', v10 = e', v12 = b'', v13 = c'', v14 = d'', v15 = e'', v17 = b''', v18 = c''', v19 = d''', v20 = e''', v21 = a, v23 = a', v25 = a'', v27 = a'''
Working v1 v6 v11 v22 v24 v26 v28 v29 v30

% Columns: "No. of Oper"; braces grouping the operations in threes;
% "Variables", the two columns each multiplication takes its factors from
% (v21 v7, v23 v2, …); "Oper"; "Quantity", the product or "a'b − 'ab = B";
% the store; an unheaded column repeating each result (B, C, D, E, 'B, …);
% braces; "Variable Cards", with the number of cards right of each group of
% three. Dashed lines across the table after operations 12 and 24. Each
% group of three is a Group here, so that its count is checked.

